# This script reads phi/psi backbone dihedral angle pairs from the input file (rama.xvg)
# and creates two Ramachandran plots:
#  1. a relative probability distribution
#  2. an approximate free energy surface
# The script first assigns all sampled phi/psi angle pairs to a two-dimensional
# histogram. The histogram is then normalized to obtain a relative probability
# distribution P(phi, psi). From this probability distribution, an approximate
# free energy surface is calculated using the Boltzmann relation:
#   F(phi, psi) = -kBT * ln(P(phi, psi))

#! pip install numpy
